  <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
  <p class="dek">Last updated November 26, 2026.</p>
  <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
  <p>At DispatchCove.com, operated by Etern Digital, we use cookies and similar technologies to operate the site, understand traffic, and run affiliate links. This policy explains what they are and how you can control them.</p>
  <h2>2. What Are Cookies?</h2>
  <p>Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you visit a website. They help a site remember information about your visit, such as a referral parameter or a preference. Similar technologies include local storage and pixels used by third parties.</p>
  <h2>3. How We Use Them</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Essential cookies and storage needed for the site to function, including remembering referral parameters on this device so an affiliate link can be attributed if you continue to a merchant.</li>
    <li>Analytics cookies, if a traffic-analytics service is enabled, to understand which pages are used.</li>
    <li>Affiliate and advertising cookies set by merchants or their networks after you click an offer link, so a later purchase can be credited.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>4. Third Parties</h2>
  <p>When you follow a link to a load board, a factoring company, a software vendor, or another third party, that company may set its own cookies under its own policy. We do not control those cookies.</p>
  <h2>5. How to Control Cookies</h2>
  <p>You can refuse or delete cookies in your browser settings. Blocking cookies may prevent some affiliate attribution and may affect how a third-party site remembers your visit. Browser help pages explain how to do this for your device.</p>
  <h2>6. Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>. See also the <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
